## 1. RedisTemplate vs @Cacheable — Which is Better?

**Neither is universally better. Use both together!**

```
@Cacheable → for method result caching
RedisTemplate → for everything else

Real project uses BOTH:

@Cacheable("users")          ← automatic cache for DB queries
redisTemplate.opsForZSet()   ← leaderboard
redisTemplate.opsForList()   ← notifications
redisTemplate.opsForValue()  ← distributed lock
```

Think of it like:
```
@Cacheable = automatic car (easy, limited)
RedisTemplate = manual car (more control, more work)

You don't throw away automatic just because manual exists!
```

