## 4. Do You Need RedisCacheManager with RedisTemplate?

**No! They are completely independent.**

```
RedisCacheManager → only needed for @Cacheable
RedisTemplate     → works on its own, needs only RedisConfig

@Cacheable uses  → RedisCacheManager
RedisTemplate    → directly talks to Redis
```

```java
// RedisTemplate only needs this:
@Bean
public RedisTemplate<String, Object> redisTemplate(
                        RedisConnectionFactory factory) {
    RedisTemplate<String, Object> template = new RedisTemplate<>();
    template.setConnectionFactory(factory);
    template.setKeySerializer(new StringRedisSerializer());
    template.setValueSerializer(new GenericJackson2JsonRedisSerializer());
    return template;
}

// RedisCacheManager only needed if you also use @Cacheable
@Bean
public RedisCacheManager cacheManager(RedisConnectionFactory factory) {
    ...
}
```

